{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-steer-terminal-child-resurrection-status-stale",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 9 of the versioned inventory (contract L7/ADR-T13-05): steering a terminal (already-settled) child resurrects it as a new turn; a collect_session(wait:false) poll issued WHILE that new turn is still in flight (deterministically gated open — the poll happens immediately after the steer's own tool dispatch, well before the gate is ever released, so there is no race about whether the new turn could have settled yet) reports the STALE first-turn result — same status/output/tokens as before the steer — not 'running' and not the new turn's own data. This is the oracle's own reproduced behavior (status lies on purpose, per L7), not a candidate defect: a later collect_session(wait:true), after the gate opens, returns the real, settled second-turn result, proving the intermediate poll really was stale rather than simply identical by coincidence.",
